:: StoryTitle
Chrono Fallout

:: Start [area:start]
You wake up in a dimly lit room. The air is damp and smells of rust. A single flickering bulb hangs from the ceiling, casting uneasy shadows across the concrete walls.

You can hear a faint humming sound coming from behind a heavy metal door to your left. To your right, a narrow corridor stretches into darkness.

[[Try the metal door (pass Strength >= 3)->metal_door_forced]]
[[Try the metal door (fail Strength < 3)->metal_door]]
[[Walk down the dark corridor->corridor]]
[[Search the room (pass Perception >= 3)->search_room_thorough]]
[[Search the room (fail Perception < 3)->search_room]]

:: metal_door [area:control_room]
You push against the metal door. It groans but gives way, slowly. Beyond it, you find a small control room filled with old monitors and blinking lights. One screen displays a map of the facility — you appear to be underground.

There's a cluttered console with blinking monitors and a half-eaten sandwich. There's another door at the far end of the control room marked 'EXIT - AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY'.

[[Search the console (pass Perception >= 3)->find_keycard]]
[[Search the console (fail Perception < 3)->console_no_keycard]]
[[Study the map on the monitor->study_map]]
[[Hack into the security system (requires Intelligence 4+)->hack_security]]
[[Go back and try the corridor instead->corridor]]

:: metal_door_forced [area:control_room]
You slam your shoulder into the metal door. It buckles and flies open with a deafening clang. Your strength surprises even you.

Beyond it, you find a small control room filled with old monitors and blinking lights. One screen displays a map of the facility — you appear to be underground.

There's a cluttered console and a door at the far end marked 'EXIT - AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY'.

[[Search the console (pass Perception >= 3)->find_keycard]]
[[Search the console (fail Perception < 3)->console_no_keycard]]
[[Study the map on the monitor->study_map]]
[[Hack into the security system (requires Intelligence 4+)->hack_security]]
[[Go back and try the corridor instead->corridor]]

:: find_keycard [area:control_room gives_item:Keycard]
Your sharp eyes spot it immediately — wedged between two monitors, a keycard with 'LEVEL 1 ACCESS' printed on it. You pocket it.

The console also has a map display and the exit door is right there.

[[Try the exit door->exit_door]]
[[Study the map on the monitor->study_map]]
[[Go back and try the corridor instead->corridor]]

:: console_no_keycard [area:control_room]
You look over the console but nothing useful catches your eye — just old coffee rings and faded paperwork. The monitors show a map and there's the exit door at the far end.

[[Try the exit door->exit_door]]
[[Study the map on the monitor->study_map]]
[[Go back and try the corridor instead->corridor]]

:: study_map [area:control_room]
The map shows three levels. You are on Level 2. Level 1 above leads to the surface exit — that must be behind the locked door. Level 3 below is marked in red with the words 'CONTAINMENT - DO NOT ENTER'.

The corridor from the starting room leads down to Level 3. A vent shaft on the map seems to connect this control room to Level 1 directly.

You also notice a small armoury marked on this level, just off the main corridor.

[[Try the exit door->exit_door]]
[[Try to find the vent shaft->vent_shaft]]
[[Search for the armoury->find_armoury]]
[[Go explore Level 3 through the corridor->corridor]]

:: hack_security [area:control_room]
You sit at the console and start working through the security system. The interface is old but familiar — military-grade encryption from the 1990s.

Your fingers fly across the keyboard. Firewalls fall. Passwords crack. Within minutes, you have full access.

The system reveals everything: floor plans, experiment logs, security camera feeds. You find a camera showing an unlocked emergency exit on this floor — just down a side hallway you hadn't noticed.

You also find a log entry: 'Subject 7 escaped containment. All personnel evacuate immediately.' The timestamp is three days ago.

[[Head to the emergency exit->exit_door]]
[[Download the experiment logs to a USB drive->download_logs]]

:: download_logs [area:control_room]
You find a USB drive in the desk drawer and start copying files. The progress bar crawls forward.

80%... 90%... 95%...

A crash echoes from somewhere deep in the facility. The lights flicker.

100%. You grab the drive and run for the emergency exit. The door opens easily and you stumble into the night.

Weeks later, the files you recovered would blow the story wide open. But for now, you just breathe the cool air and walk toward the distant glow of a town.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: find_armoury [area:control_room gives_item:Gun]
You follow the map's markings down a short side corridor. Behind a reinforced door — thankfully unlocked — you find a small armoury. Most of the racks are empty, but a single pistol remains, along with a magazine of ammunition.

You check the chamber, load it, and tuck the gun into your waistband. It's heavy and cold against your back, but reassuring.

[[Head back to the control room->metal_door]]
[[Go explore Level 3 through the corridor->corridor]]

:: exit_door [area:control_room]
You reach the heavy door marked 'EXIT - AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY'. A keycard reader blinks red beside it.

[[Swipe the keycard (requires Keycard)->exit_escape]]
[[Go back — you need to find a keycard->metal_door]]

:: exit_escape [area:control_room]
You swipe the keycard. A green light blinks and the heavy door slides open with a hiss. Cold night air rushes in.

You step outside onto a hillside overlooking a quiet valley bathed in moonlight. You're free. Behind you, the facility hums on, indifferent to your escape.

You take a deep breath and walk into the night.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: corridor [area:corridors]
You step into the corridor. The darkness swallows you almost immediately. You trail your hand along the cold wall to guide yourself.

After what feels like minutes, you reach a fork. A faint blue glow pulses from the left path. The right path carries the distant echo of dripping water.

[[Follow the blue glow->blue_glow]]
[[Follow the sound of water->water_path]]
[[Listen carefully for other sounds (requires Perception 5+)->hidden_passage]]
[[Turn back to the starting room->Start]]

:: blue_glow [area:corridors]
You follow the blue glow and enter a vast underground chamber. Luminescent fungi cover the walls, painting everything in an eerie blue light.

In the center of the chamber sits a strange crystalline structure, pulsing gently. As you approach, you feel a warmth in your chest and hear whispers at the edge of your mind.

The crystal seems to be calling to you.

[[Touch the crystal->touch_crystal]]
[[Back away and take the water path->water_path]]

:: touch_crystal [area:corridors]
You reach out and touch the crystal. A surge of energy courses through you. Visions flash before your eyes — the facility being built, experiments, people in lab coats, something escaping containment.

When the visions fade, you realize you can sense the layout of the entire facility. Every door, every path, every exit is clear in your mind.

But you also sense something else. Something on Level 3. And it knows you're here now.

[[Rush to the nearest exit — the water path->water_path]]
[[Descend to Level 3 to face whatever is down there->level_3]]

:: water_path [area:corridors]
You follow the sound of water. The tunnel opens into a natural cave where an underground stream flows steadily toward a crack of pale light in the distance.

The water is knee-deep and cold, but the light ahead is unmistakable — it's daylight. You wade forward, and the crack widens into an opening.

You emerge at the base of a cliff, squinting in the morning sun. You're free.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: hidden_passage [area:corridors]
You close your eyes and listen. Beyond the blue hum and the dripping water, you catch something else — a faint draft of warm air, coming from a crack in the wall.

You feel along the rock and find a narrow gap, just wide enough to squeeze through. Beyond it is a forgotten maintenance tunnel, still lit by emergency strips on the floor.

The tunnel leads steadily upward. After ten minutes of walking, you push through a rusted door and find yourself on the surface — a moonlit clearing in a forest.

No alarms. No creatures. Just silence and freedom.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: vent_shaft [area:garage]
You locate the vent shaft behind a panel in the control room. It's a tight fit, but you pull yourself through.

The shaft climbs steeply. Your arms burn but you keep going. After a grueling climb, you kick out a grate and tumble onto a concrete floor.

You're in a garage. A rusted truck sits by a large roller door. Moonlight seeps through the cracks.

[[Pry the roller door open with brute force (requires Strength 5+)->exit_door]]
[[Try to open the roller door->exit_door]]
[[Search the truck->search_truck]]

:: search_truck [area:garage]
The truck's cabin is unlocked. Inside you find keys in the ignition and a map with a route marked to a nearby town. But the garage roller door has an electronic lock — it needs a keycard to open.

[[Swipe the keycard and drive out (requires Keycard)->truck_escape]]
[[Go back — you need to find a keycard->metal_door]]

:: truck_escape [area:garage]
You swipe the keycard on the roller door panel. It beeps and the door grinds upward, revealing a dirt road under a star-filled sky.

You turn the key. The engine coughs, sputters, then roars to life. The fuel gauge reads half-full.

You drive into the night, leaving the facility behind for good.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: level_3 [area:level_3]
You descend deeper into the facility. Level 3 is colder. The lights here are red and most are broken.

At the end of a long hallway, you find a massive containment chamber. The glass is shattered. Whatever was held here is long gone.

But on the floor, scratched into the metal, are the words: 'WE SHOULD NEVER HAVE DUG THIS DEEP.'

A sound behind you. Breathing. Not your own.

[[Raise your gun and fire (requires Gun)->shoot_creature]]
[[Stand your ground and face the creature (requires Endurance 5+)->face_creature]]
[[Sprint for the exit (requires Agility 4+)->sprint_exit]]
[[Run in a panic->panic_run]]

:: shoot_creature [area:level_3 uses_item:Gun]
You spin around, gun already raised. In the red half-light you see it — a towering, gaunt figure with too-long arms and skin like cracked stone.

It lunges. You fire.

The shot echoes through the corridor like thunder. The creature staggers, shrieks — a sound like tearing metal — and collapses. It twitches once, then goes still.

Your hands are shaking. But it's dead. You step over the body and find a maintenance ladder behind the containment chamber.

You climb. You climb until you see sky.

You emerge into cold, sweet air. Whatever that thing was, it won't follow anyone else.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: face_creature [area:level_3]
You steel yourself and turn around. In the red half-light, you see it — a towering, gaunt figure with too-long arms and skin like cracked stone.

It tilts its head. Studying you. You don't flinch.

Minutes pass. Or maybe hours. Then it steps aside, revealing a passage behind it — one not on any map. The creature watches as you walk through.

The passage leads to a ladder. The ladder leads to the sky.

You emerge into dawn, forever changed by what you faced below.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: sprint_exit [area:level_3]
Your reflexes kick in before your fear does. You pivot and sprint — ducking under pipes, vaulting over debris, taking corners at full speed.

The breathing follows you, but you're faster. You burst through door after door, up staircases, through a final fire exit —

Cold air. Stars. Grass under your feet.

You don't stop until your legs give out on a hillside, the facility far behind you.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: panic_run [area:level_3]
You run. You run faster than you've ever run, through corridors that blur together, up stairs, through doors — until you burst outside into cold, sweet air.

You don't stop running until the facility is just a dot on the horizon. You're alive, but shaken to your core.

[[Play again->Start]]

:: search_room [area:start]
You fumble around the room but don't find much of use. The walls are bare and the floor seems solid. Nothing here but dust and shadows.

[[Try the metal door->metal_door]]
[[Head into the corridor->corridor]]

:: search_room_thorough [area:start gives_item:Flashlight]
Your sharp senses guide you. You notice a loose floor tile that others might miss. Underneath, you find a flashlight — still working — and a crumpled note.

The note reads: 'If you're reading this, don't trust the blue light. The water is the way out. - M'

You pocket the flashlight and the note.

[[Try the metal door->metal_door]]
[[Head into the corridor with your flashlight->corridor]]
